<title>CHINA: New China gold project to produce 2.0 tonnes/yr.</title>
<headline>New China gold project to produce 2.0 tonnes/yr.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>China has approved a new gold project in the northwestern region of Xinjiang that would produce up to 2.0 tonnes of gold a year, the People's Daily Overseas Edition said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The 13th Engineering Bureau under the Ministry of Railways would handle actual mining of the mine in Axi and the Axi Gold Bureau would handle ore dressing, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>The mine was expected to have an output of 1.75 to 2.0 tonnes a year, it said but gave no further details.</p>
<p>China's gold production was 108 tonnes in 1995 and output is exepected to rise to 115 tonnes in 1996.</p>
</text>
